# OneOS Phase 1 base package set.
#
# Deliberately minimal. Every package here must justify itself against the
# 4 GB / dual-core minimum spec. Nothing in this file is a desktop component --
# the compositor and shell arrive in Phases 2 and 3 and get their own list.

# --- Live session ------------------------------------------------------------
# These MUST be listed explicitly. live-build pulls in live-boot and
# live-config on its own, but live-config-systemd is only a Recommends of
# live-config -- and we build with --apt-recommends false, so it was silently
# dropped.
#
# Without live-config-systemd not one live-config component runs at boot, which
# means the live user named in --bootappend-live is never created. The symptom
# is a login screen with an empty user list and no way in: the system boots
# perfectly and is completely unusable.
live-boot
live-config
live-config-systemd

# --- Boot and init -----------------------------------------------------------
systemd
systemd-sysv
systemd-timesyncd
systemd-resolved
# NOTE: dracut must NOT be listed here, even though docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
# prefers it. A live ISO boots via live-boot-initramfs-tools, which depends on
# initramfs-tools, and dracut Provides/Conflicts linux-initramfs-tool. Listing
# both makes the package solver fail with "held broken packages".
# initramfs-tools arrives automatically as a live-boot dependency.
# The switch to dracut belongs in Phase 6, when the base moves to an
# mkosi-built A/B image that has no live-boot component at all.
# Stock Debian kernel for Phase 1. Replaced by the OneOS kernel package in
# Phase 1b -- see kernel/README.md.
linux-image-amd64
firmware-linux-free
# non-free-firmware: required for the Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and GPU hardware that
# actually ships in consumer laptops. Without these the OS is unusable on most
# real machines. This is a pragmatic exception to the open-source-only rule and
# it is the same choice Debian itself made in Debian 12.
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-misc-nonfree
intel-microcode
amd64-microcode

# --- Boot chain --------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: systemd-boot must NOT be listed here. Its postinst runs `bootctl
# install`, which requires a real mounted EFI System Partition. There is none
# inside a live-build chroot, so dpkg fails and takes the whole build with it.
# The live ISO is booted by syslinux/grub-efi, which live-build installs into
# the image itself -- no chroot package needed.
# systemd-boot belongs to the installed system in Phase 6, where the A/B image
# is built by mkosi against a real ESP.
efibootmgr
cryptsetup
cryptsetup-initramfs
lvm2

# --- Filesystems -------------------------------------------------------------
e2fsprogs
dosfstools
btrfs-progs
exfatprogs
ntfs-3g
fuse3

# --- Networking --------------------------------------------------------------
network-manager
wpasupplicant
iproute2
iputils-ping
ca-certificates
openssh-client

# --- Hardware / power --------------------------------------------------------
pciutils
usbutils
udisks2
upower
fwupd
bluez
zram-tools

# --- Core userland -----------------------------------------------------------
bash
coreutils
util-linux
sudo
polkitd
less
nano
vim-tiny
curl
wget
gnupg
apt-transport-https

# --- Diagnostics (keep: you will need these on the test laptops) -------------
htop
strace
lsof
tree
